To completely disable the declaration of DTDs and protect against XML External Entity (XXE) attacks in a Java application using `DocumentBuilderFactory`, you need to set the following feature to `true`:

```java
DocumentBuilderFactory factory = DocumentBuilderFactory.newInstance();
factory.setFeature("http://apache.org/xml/features/disallow-doctype-decl", true);
```

This feature, `http://apache.org/xml/features/disallow-doctype-decl`, when set to `true`, disallows the declaration of DOCTYPE and external DTDs, effectively preventing XXE attacks.
